---
# Bulk manage — the several-records-at-once screen.
#
# A page of our own rather than something grafted into Decap's collection list.
# Decap 3.15.1 registers widgets, previews, backends, media libraries, locales,
# event listeners and custom formats — and nothing else. There is no documented
# way to add a page, a route, a sidebar entry or a list action, so the only way
# to put checkboxes into its collection list would be to reach into generated
# class names and internal state, which this repository has already learned not
# to do. See docs/CMS_BULK_MANAGE.md §2.
#
# Emitted ONLY when CMS_DEV=1, exactly like the admin entry point beside it, so
# no public build can ever produce it.
permalink: /admin/bulk/index.html
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow, noarchive, noimageindex" />
    <title>Bulk manage — Federation Content Manager</title>
    <style>
{{ cmsConfig.bulkStyles | safe }}
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <p class="cms-local-banner">
      Local development only — changes are written straight to the files in your
      working copy. Nothing here is published. Review with
      <code>git diff</code> before committing.
    </p>

    <header class="bulk-header">
      <a class="bulk-back" href="/admin/">&larr; Content manager</a>
      <h1>Bulk manage</h1>
      <p class="bulk-intro">
        Hide, show or delete several records at once. Hiding is reversible;
        deleting is not.
      </p>
    </header>

    <main class="bulk" id="bulk-app">
      <noscript>
        <p class="bulk-note">This screen needs JavaScript.</p>
      </noscript>
    </main>

    <script>
{{ cmsConfig.bulkScript | safe }}
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
